DOCUMENT();
loadMacros("PGstandard.pl", "MathObjects.pl", "PGML.pl", "contextFraction.pl");
TEXT(beginproblem());

Context("Fraction");

$a = random(2, 5, 1);
$b = random(1, 3, 1);
$f1 = Fraction($a, $b);
$f2 = Fraction($b, $a);
$sum = $f1 + $f2;

Context("Numeric");
$decimal = Real($sum);

BEGIN_PGML
# Comprehensive Demo Problem

This problem tests multiple macro systems working together.

## Fraction Operations

Given two fractions:
* [`f_1 = \frac{[$a]}{[$b]}`]
* [`f_2 = \frac{[$b]}{[$a]}`]

### Questions

1. What is [`f_1 + f_2`] as a fraction? [_____]{$sum}

2. What is this sum as a decimal? [_____]{$decimal}

---

### Visual Elements

${BBOLD}Bold text${EBOLD} and ${BITALIC}italic text${EITALIC}$BR
$BR
Horizontal rule:$BR
\{HR()\}
$BR
Line break: \{BR()\} done.

END_PGML

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION
# Solution

## Step 1: Add fractions

[```\frac{[$a]}{[$b]} + \frac{[$b]}{[$a]} = \frac{[$a] \cdot [$a] + [$b] \cdot [$b]}{[$a] \cdot [$b]} = [$sum]```]

## Step 2: Convert to decimal

[```[$sum] = [$decimal]```]

END_PGML_SOLUTION

ENDDOCUMENT();

